§ CSLv3 GRAMMAR
I> reconciled: pasted (CFG + LL(2)), root (PEG), specs/ (BNF + slot grammar)
R! ← Lojban: unambiguous parse via rigid word-class markers
R! ← J: ASCII fallback everywhere
W! LL(2) target — parseable w/ 2-token lookahead
W! ∄ ambiguous parse — if two readings: mandatory explicit grouping

§ TOKEN CLASSES
  GLYPH   → single unicode sigil (table §01)
  WORD    → [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]* (identifiers, densified nouns)
  NUM     → integer | float | hex (0x) | bin (0b)
  STR     → "..." | `...` (raw)
  SUFFIX  → 'd | 'f | 's | 't | 'e | 'm | 'p | 'g | 'r (determinative)

§ SLOT TEMPLATE
I> from v2-specs, most formalized slot grammar
I> every CSLv3 statement occupies:
  [EVIDENCE?] [MODAL?] [DET?] SUBJECT [RELATION] OBJECT [GATE?] [SCOPE?] [META?]

| slot     | pos | required | default         | content                    |
|----------|-----|----------|-----------------|----------------------------|
| EVIDENCE | 0   | ○        | ✓ (confirmed)   | ✓ ◐ ○ ✗ ⊘ △ ▽ ‼            |
| MODAL    | 1   | ○        | (assertion)     | W! R! M? N! I> Q? P> D>    |
| DET      | 2   | ○        | (none)          | § ∫ ⊞ or type suffix       |
| SUBJECT  | 3   | ✓        | —               | compound name              |
| RELATION | 4   | ✓        | : (is/has)      | : :: = → ← ↔ ∈ ⊂ ≡        |
| OBJECT   | 5   | ✓        | —               | value/type/target          |
| GATE     | 6   | ○        | (unconditional) | if/when/unless + expr      |
| SCOPE    | 7   | ○        | (global)        | @frame, @chunk, per entity |
| META     | 8   | ○        | (none)          | # comment                  |

§ SLOT OMISSION RULES (Ithkuil: defaults are silent)
  slot 0 omitted → ✓ (confirmed/certain)
  slot 1 omitted → assertion (not modal)
  slot 4 omitted → : (definition/binding)
  slot 6 omitted → unconditional
  slot 7 omitted → global scope
  W! only write non-default values

§ LINE STRUCTURE (Caveman rule)
  DROP: articles (a/an/the), auxiliaries (is/are/was),
        copulas where inferable, filler (that/which),
        "in order to", "it is important", "note that"
  KEEP: nouns, verbs, relationships, numbers, gates, glyphs
  ORDER: topic → relation → object (SVO collapse when unambiguous)

§ BLOCK STRUCTURE
  colon + indent = scope introduction (Python-like)
  §HEADER:
    content
    content
  ∎  § optional explicit close; indentation-sensitive otherwise
  
  W! indent = scope boundary (Peircean cut linearized)
  W! adjacent items at same indent = conjoined (Peircean juxtaposition)

§ PARSE PRIORITY (high → low)
  glyph-prefix   § @ # & * $
  enclosure       ( ) [ ] { } ⟨ ⟩ ⟦ ⟧ « » ⌈ ⌉ ⌊ ⌋ ⟪ ⟫
  postfix-suffix  'd 'f 's 't 'e 'm 'p 'g 'r
  unary           ¬ ~ !
  access          . :: 
  binary-arith    * / %  +  -
  range           ..
  binary-cmp      < > ≤ ≥ = ≠ ≈
  binary-logic    ∧ ∨ ⊕
  binary-flow     → ← ⇒ ↔ |> <|
  binary-meta     ⊢ ∴ ∵ ~>
  conditional     ? :
  sequence        , ;

§ BNF GRAMMAR (unified from 3 v2 grammars)
```bnf
document     ::= section*
section      ::= '§'+ ident ':' INDENT block DEDENT
block        ::= statement*

statement    ::= evidence? modal? definition
              |  evidence? modal? relation_stmt
              |  evidence? modal? constraint
              |  evidence? modal? conditional
              |  formula
              |  directive
              |  comment

evidence     ::= '✓' | '◐' | '○' | '✗' | '⊘' | '△' | '▽' | '‼'
modal        ::= 'W!' | 'R!' | 'M?' | 'N!' | 'I>' | 'Q?' | 'P>' | 'D>'

definition   ::= subject ':' type_expr constraint? scope? meta?
              |  subject '=' expr scope? meta?
              |  'def' ident suffix? '{' field* '}'
              |  'def' ident suffix? '=' 'enum' '[' variant_list ']'
              |  'fn' ident '(' params? ')' ('->' type_expr)? body

relation_stmt::= subject rel_op object gate? scope? meta?
rel_op       ::= '→' | '←' | '↔' | '⇒' | '∈' | '⊂' | '::' | '≡'

constraint   ::= '⌈' expr '⌉'
              |  '⌊' expr '⌋'
formula      ::= '⟦' (!'⟧' .)* '⟧'
conditional  ::= expr ':' INDENT block DEDENT
              |  expr '→' expr
              |  expr '?' expr ':' expr

subject      ::= det? compound suffix?
object       ::= det? compound suffix? | literal | type_expr | block_expr
det          ::= '§' | '∫' | '⊞'

compound     ::= atom ('.' atom)*
              |  compound '+' compound
              |  compound '-' compound
              |  compound '⊗' compound
              |  compound '@' compound
atom         ::= WORD | '$' DIGIT

suffix       ::= "'" [dfstemgpr]

type_expr    ::= prim_type | array_type | union_type | opt_type
              |  tuple_type | map_type | ref_type | result_type
prim_type    ::= 'f32' | 'f64' | 'i32' | 'i64' | 'u8' | 'u16' | 'u32' | 'u64'
              |  'bool' | 'vec2' | 'vec3' | 'vec4' | 'mat4' | 'quat' | 'str'
array_type   ::= '[' type_expr ';' (NUM | '_') ']'
union_type   ::= type_expr '|' type_expr
opt_type     ::= type_expr '?'
result_type  ::= type_expr '!'
tuple_type   ::= '(' type_expr (',' type_expr)* ')'
map_type     ::= '{' type_expr ':' type_expr '}'
ref_type     ::= '&' type_expr

gate         ::= ('if' | 'when' | 'unless' | 'while') expr
scope        ::= ('@' compound) | ('per' compound) | ('in' compound)
meta         ::= '#' TEXT_TO_EOL
comment      ::= '#' TEXT_TO_EOL | '§{' TEXT '§}'
directive    ::= modal TEXT_TO_EOL

literal      ::= NUM | STR | 'true' | 'false' | 'nil'
body         ::= '{' statement* expr? '}'
block_expr   ::= '{' statement* expr? '}'
field        ::= ident suffix? '::' type_expr constraint? meta?
variant_list ::= ident (',' ident)*
              |  ident '{' variant_list '}' (',' variant_list)*
params       ::= param (',' param)*
param        ::= ident '::' type_expr
args         ::= expr (',' expr)*
expr         ::= term (op term)*
term         ::= compound | literal | '(' expr ')' | '¬' term
              |  fn_call | lambda | pipeline
fn_call      ::= ident '(' args? ')'
lambda       ::= 'λ' '(' params? ')' '→' expr
              |  '\\' '(' params? ')' '->' expr
pipeline     ::= expr ('|>' expr)+
op           ::= '+' | '-' | '*' | '/' | '%'
              |  '==' | '!=' | '<' | '>' | '<=' | '>='
              |  '∧' | '∨' | '⊕' | '&' | '|'

INDENT       ::= (increase in indentation, 2 spaces per level)
DEDENT       ::= (decrease in indentation)
```

§ DE BRUIJN POSITIONAL REFERENCE
I> from v2-root: within scope block (3 levels max), $0 $1 $2 replace names
  $0 = first defined thing in scope
  $1 = second
  $2 = third
  W! beyond 3 levels or cross-scope → use names
  W! positional ref = local optimization, ¬ mandatory
∎
